p.src:
To construct a Lagrangian we introduce the vector potential $\bm A(\bm x)$, defined by $\bm B=\bm\nabla\times\bm A.$ In components, $\begin{aligned}
 B_x&=\frac{\partial A_z}{\partial y}
     -\frac{\partial A_y}{\partial z},\notag\\
 B_y&=\frac{\partial A_x}{\partial z}
     -\frac{\partial A_z}{\partial x},\notag\\
 B_z&=\frac{\partial A_y}{\partial x}
     -\frac{\partial A_x}{\partial y}.
 \end{aligned}$ Writing a field as a curl automatically gives $\bm\nabla\cdot\bm B=0$, the absence of magnetic monopole sources in the classical theory being used here.

