p.src:
The Hamiltonian in canonical variables is therefore $\boxed{
 H(\bm x,\bm p)
 =\frac{1}{2m}\bigl(\bm p-q\bm A(\bm x)\bigr)^2.}$ It looks more complicated than the kinetic energy because the canonical momentum contains the vector potential. The combination $\bm p-q\bm A=m\bm v$ is the mechanical momentum.

